      "writtenOn": "2021-05-17T10:00:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure we can handle input and output devices connection with the same isConnected booleans. What happens if we have an output device connected with the same address of a newly connected input device?\nWe need to clarify and document the expected behavior fo the BLE stack: how doe sit handle device connection? Do we have 2 separate notifications to audio service like for BT SCO (one for input , one for output)? Is it possible that a headset is first activated for output only and then for input (via bluetooth settings or other)?\nIt maybe clearer to have separate APIs (or an argument) for input and output LE audio devices like we have for A2DP source and A2DP sink.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 491,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 491,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "1f8de0db3de361d550ba5798d889e3fde81aa85c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f44d7c18_273455e4",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/audio/AudioDeviceInventory.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687135
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-24T13:35:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the problems with fitting LE Audio to current API is device context.\nIn most cases, devices are represented by group e.g. Left earbud with bd address \u0027A\u0027 (with input and output), Right earbud with bd address - \u0027B\u0027 (with input only) are in one group - let\u0027s call it \"1\".\nIdea here was to present whole group which may cover a input and output \"device\" under some bluetooth address e.g. \u0027A\u0027 (from LE Audio device group).\n\nSummary:\n1) How to deal with device context for LE Audio groups ?\n2) In case of split to in and out \"devices\" - how pick in or out \"device\" from audio device picker. Both of them would be under the same address.",
      "parentUuid": "80a58de5_42acebf7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 491,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 491,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "1f8de0db3de361d550ba5798d889e3fde81aa85c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e15e01e9_d1fd9e1c",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/audio/AudioDeviceInventory.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-25T13:08:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should simply handle input and output devices separately like we do for SCO and A2DP\n\nThe device picker so far only handles output devices. So this will be the same for BLE audio. For media this is straightforward. For communication, this works because the call routing logic and APIs in AudioService expect an output device as the route selection even if the audio policy has rule to match the input and output devices based on only the output device selection.",
      "parentUuid": "f44d7c18_273455e4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 491,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 491,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "1f8de0db3de361d550ba5798d889e3fde81aa85c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
